  "question": {
    "text": "An alpha- particle of mass <math><mi>m</mi></math> suffers <math><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">-</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></math> dimensional elastic collision with a nucleus at rest of unknown mass. It is scattered directly backwards losing <math><mn>64</mn><mi>%</mi></math> of its initial kinetic energy. The mass of the nucleus is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "2PIpZ",
